 "inference": [
  "For the site, precedence is moot on 2.1.1.0: every paired row on the 67 weapons is equal, and attachment-effect files have no registry row to compete with.",
  "AAHV heat cannot discriminate the sources: 8 vs 8 shots at capacity 1.0 without cooling; the 1-shot differences need unproven boundary or cooling rules.",
  "The 720 row appears unbound to M16A3_WB (its group node is imported by nothing), the PB_C4 pattern; this is an import-graph inference, not runtime proof.",
  "The M136 AT zoomed standing-stationary MinAngle (file 0.0, registry 0.35, group imported by GS_AT4) is the cleanest controlled in-game discriminator found (operator-check.md)."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Runtime precedence itself: no source fact shows which value the game uses for a bound row; operator-check.md is the proposed test.",
  "Whether the 720 'M16A3_WB - InitialSpeed.z' row is read at runtime: like every value row it is imported only by TweakablesConfig, and it hangs from a group node no raw file imports; runtime binding by label is not shown.",
  "AAHV shots to overheat depend on unstored capacity (1.0 assumed), the >= vs > boundary and whether cooling runs between shots; 8 vs 8 in the plain model.",
  "MinAngle units and that it is the first-shot aimed spread are inferred from the label, not proven.",
  "524 array-valued rows on site owners (damage curves, ReloadTimerArray, recoil-by-order) are not scalar-paired here; curves were paired in the 19 Oct curves.py run.",
  "20 catalog-only attachment-effect routes (16 WPM_, 4 GDM_) are not in the raw tree; their registry check is by name only (needs capture only if their contents matter)."
 ],
 "siteImpact": "None. On 2.1.1.0 the registry default equals the own value on every paired row of the 67 site weapons (15,879 values: 2,771/11,524/567 on the 63, 141/824/52 on the four Season 5 weapons), so site numbers are the same under a registry-first or file-first rule. The six generators emit no stat on an owner with a difference. The 98 differing pairs and the AAHV, minigun and M16 odd rows touch no site weapon. Conditional: if the operator check shows the file wins, only future vehicle/gadget pages and the registry-first choices in VEHICLES.md/GADGETS.md are affected.",
 "outOfScopeNotes": [
  "VEHICLES.md L3373 test 'count Scout Helicopter minigun shots to overheat (112 or 150)' cannot run as written: file and registry both store a 100-round magazine; 0.008889 also gives 113, not 112, at capacity 1.0.",
